{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"ed70c4ba6d8e3036","type":"group","x":-340,"y":-3320,"width":480,"height":488,"label":"Video Lecture"},
		{"id":"agre_split","type":"text","text":"**Split Identity**\nThe critical programmer holds two roles at once: the *making foot* builds the system; the *critical foot* watches what the system assumes. Neither cancels the other.","x":-480,"y":-2120,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"agre_anchor","type":"text","text":"## Agre\n*Critical Technical Practice*","x":-200,"y":-2360,"width":260,"height":80,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"sub_mag","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 03 - Epistemic Tools + Entanglement/submodules/DIGM 553 - W03A - Magnusson — Epistemic Tools.md","x":-2520,"y":-1560,"width":800,"height":360,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"37c797a464a728e3","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 03 - Epistemic Tools + Entanglement/media/Pasted image 20260414083657.png","x":-2640,"y":-2440,"width":560,"height":448},
		{"id":"4cf025d2d31dcd69","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 03 - Epistemic Tools + Entanglement/media/Pasted image 20260414083828.png","x":-3440,"y":-2040,"width":720,"height":571},
		{"id":"2a32d0855464227e","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 03 - Epistemic Tools + Entanglement/media/Pasted image 20260414084026.png","x":-2320,"y":-2880,"width":400,"height":356},
		{"id":"86f9a10a10f44a48","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 03 - Epistemic Tools + Entanglement/media/Pythagoras-conceived-the-universe-as-an-immense-monochord-with-its-single-string.png","x":-3680,"y":-1240,"width":840,"height":455},
		{"id":"week_title","type":"text","text":"# Week 3 — Epistemic Tools + Entanglement\n*What does your tool think? Where are you inside it? Where does it break?*","x":-420,"y":-2680,"width":680,"height":100,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"b5f483bf828df743","type":"link","url":"https://vimeo.com/1183037079?share=copy&fl=sv&fe=ci","x":-300,"y":-3300,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"workshop","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 03 - Epistemic Tools + Entanglement/submodules/DIGM 553 - W03D - Epistemic Tool Audit Workshop.md","x":-800,"y":440,"width":520,"height":360},
		{"id":"eta_template","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Documents/Tool Audit — Template + Guide.md","x":-240,"y":440,"width":520,"height":360},
		{"id":"proposal_template","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Documents/Speculative Proposal — Template + Guide.md","x":320,"y":440,"width":520,"height":360},
		{"id":"agre_imperialism","type":"text","text":"**Computational Imperialism**\nWhen a tool exports its worldview — formalizing what counts as ‘input,’ ‘event,’ ‘response’ — it starts colonizing the phenomena it was built to describe.","x":120,"y":-2160,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"dq4","type":"text","text":"**Q:** Where in your signal chain do you stop being a *user* and become part of the *apparatus*?","x":280,"y":-440,"width":380,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dq1","type":"text","text":"**Q:** What is one default in your current tools you have *stopped questioning*? What did it assume when you absorbed it?","x":-1040,"y":-440,"width":380,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dq2","type":"text","text":"**Q:** Where is your *split identity* live right now — where are you simultaneously building and critiquing?","x":-600,"y":-440,"width":380,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dq3","type":"text","text":"**Q:** Name one moment your tool *failed or glitched*. What did that failure reveal about what the tool assumes?","x":-160,"y":-440,"width":380,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"convergence","type":"text","text":"### The Audit\nYour apparatus — *as a whole* — believes the world is made of certain things and not others. Today’s work: make that belief visible before it makes you.\n\n*What does it know? What does it amplify? What does it discard?*","x":-360,"y":-40,"width":760,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"263750c787ef56be","type":"text","text":"https://vimeo.com/1183037079?share=copy&fl=sv&fe=ci","x":-320,"y":-2940,"width":440,"height":88},
		{"id":"mag_ampred","type":"text","text":"**Amplification / Reduction**\nTools make some things easy and some things impossible. ","x":-1160,"y":-1960,"width":300,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"barad_industry","type":"text","text":"**Studio Pulse — Barad**\nBluecadet’s interactive installations: when visitor body + sensor + projection co-produce an event, there is an intra-action. The visitors become part of the apparatus.","x":1040,"y":-1240,"width":300,"height":240,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"agre_invisible","type":"text","text":"**Invisible Architecture**\nThe most powerful design decisions are the ones you stop seeing. What have you naturalized in your signal chain without examining?","x":-160,"y":-1800,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"dq5","type":"text","text":"**Q:** What does your tool discard in the service of a ‘clean signal’? Is that discard compositional material?","x":720,"y":-440,"width":380,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"cross_worldview","type":"text","text":"**All three agree:** tools embed worldviews. The question is whether you can see yours from inside it.","x":0,"y":-1180,"width":440,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cross_failure","type":"text","text":"**Failure as data**\nAgre: stay with the bad connection. Barad: the apparatus produces what it excludes. Magnusson: what the tool can’t hear tells you what it thinks the world is.","x":-280,"y":-720,"width":440,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"agre_industry","type":"text","text":"**Studio Pulse — Agre**\nbrdg.studio: their practice *builds* the computational logic in the room and asks what worldview it will present before deploying it in public space.","x":-320,"y":-1440,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"48a75fdc0eedeebc","type":"link","url":"https://www.poetickinetics.com","x":1200,"y":-400,"width":880,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"c6e6a601ee5ed2f1","type":"link","url":"https://www.arts.ac.uk/creative-computing-institute","x":1200,"y":60,"width":880,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"8c2ec9dcd4e2933e","type":"link","url":"https://www.lozano-hemmer.com","x":1200,"y":480,"width":880,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"mag_industry","type":"text","text":"**Studio Pulse — Magnusson**\nMeow Wolf builds environments where *the architecture is the interface.* Every ramp, doorframe, and texture is an epistemic tool,  it decides what counts as ‘up,’ ‘in,’ ‘weird.’","x":-1400,"y":-1280,"width":300,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"sub_barad","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 03 - Epistemic Tools + Entanglement/submodules/DIGM 553 - W03C - Barad — Entanglement and Intra-action.md","x":1560,"y":-1480,"width":800,"height":400,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"c22557ff86247ed8","type":"link","url":"https://meowwolf.com","x":-2520,"y":-1140,"width":800,"height":600,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"89756009a975a1da","type":"link","url":"https://www.bluecadet.com","x":1560,"y":-1040,"width":800,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cross_body","type":"text","text":"**Whose body?**\nMagnusson’s amplification, Agre’s marginalization, Barad’s apparatus — they all circle the same question: *whose context was imagined when this was built?*","x":20,"y":-960,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"d38dbf54d74c5047","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 03 - Epistemic Tools + Entanglement/media/Pasted image 20260414082903.png","x":1720,"y":-2200,"width":793,"height":460},
		{"id":"6e6c9e3901fd34af","type":"link","url":"https://newmaterialism.eu/almanac/a/agential-cut.html","x":2640,"y":-1880,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"94da80bae5f5d736","type":"link","url":"https://newmaterialism.eu/almanac/a/apparatus.html","x":2640,"y":-1400,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"67e3df80e9d8a01c","type":"link","url":"https://newmaterialism.eu/almanac/i/intra-action.html","x":2480,"y":-2720,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"f979bd80f675abc8","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 03 - Epistemic Tools + Entanglement/media/Screenshot-e1585243380975-2281196920.png","x":1520,"y":-2800,"width":520,"height":384},
		{"id":"mag_blackbox","type":"text","text":"**Black Boxes**\nEvery tool is a crystallized argument. When you stop questioning the default, the designer's choice becomes invisible, and starts shaping yours.","x":-1600,"y":-1960,"width":300,"height":240,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"mag_ihde","type":"text","text":"**Ihde’s Modalities**\n*Embodiment* — tool disappears into use\n*Hermeneutic* — tool mediates interpretation\n*Alterity* — tool becomes an ‘other’ you relate to","x":-1400,"y":-1600,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"barad_intra","type":"text","text":"**Intra-action vs. Interaction**\nInteraction assumes two things that pre-exist and then meet. Intra-action: *the things emerge through the meeting.* You and your tool are not separate before you begin.","x":840,"y":-1920,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"barad_agential","type":"text","text":"**Agential Cuts**\nEvery threshold, confidence floor, and silence gap is a cut. Cuts are decision about what counts as signal and what gets discarded. Cuts enact boundaries.","x":1040,"y":-1580,"width":300,"height":220,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"barad_anchor","type":"text","text":"## Barad\n*Entanglement + Intra-action*","x":1040,"y":-2320,"width":260,"height":80,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"mag_anchor","type":"text","text":"## Magnusson\n*Epistemic Tools*","x":-1360,"y":-2280,"width":260,"height":80,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"sub_agre","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 03 - Epistemic Tools + Entanglement/submodules/DIGM 553 - W03B - Agre — Critical Technical Practice.md","x":-1880,"y":-320,"width":720,"height":320,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"5fa4e131a2c1a566","type":"link","url":"https://brdg.co","x":-1880,"y":40,"width":720,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"88c62c231f104513","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 03 - Epistemic Tools + Entanglement/media/Pasted image 20260414084208.png","x":-1400,"y":-2960,"width":711,"height":400},
		{"id":"a911b324d40a18cf","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 03 - Epistemic Tools + Entanglement/media/bLxtp8rUsHNb4kBlLoOAxz9vO0-3213374487.png","x":-2080,"y":-3680,"width":1040,"height":585},
		{"id":"barad_apparatus","type":"text","text":"**The Apparatus**\nNot a neutral recorder of reality but a *material-discursive practice* that produces the phenomena it studies. Your hydrophone + Max patch + corpus = one apparatus with one worldview.","x":1240,"y":-1920,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"5"}
	],
